-- title:
--   Finiteness of the flat deformation tangent space
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a commutative local ring whose residue field $k =$ `ResidueField 𝒪` is finite, let $\bar\rho$ be a residual representation over $k$ in the project's sense ([`ResidualGaloisRep`](def/GaloisRep_Residual.html#L22): a $k$-vector space $V$ of dimension $2$ together with a monoid homomorphism from $\mathrm{Aut}_{\mathbb{Q}}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ to $\mathrm{End}_k(V)$ satisfying the project predicate [`GaloisFactorsThroughFiniteLevel`](def/GaloisRep_Residual.html#L17)), and let $p$ be a natural number and $S$ a finite set of natural numbers — no primality is assumed of $p$ and no condition is imposed on the members of $S$. The theorem asserts `TangentFinite 𝒪 ρbar (flatCondition 𝒪 p S)`. Unfolding the two project notions: `flatCondition 𝒪 p S` is the conjunction, for a representation $\rho$ over an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra local ring $A$, of (i) `DetIsCyclotomic p` (that $p \in \mathfrak{m}_A$ and that $\det\rho$ agrees with the cyclotomic character modulo $p^n$ for every $n$), (ii) `IsFlatAt p` (that $A$ has finite residue field and that each finite-level quotient $\rho.V/I\rho.V$ is realised, Galois-equivariantly and additively, by the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points of a finite flat cocommutative Hopf algebra over the subring `ratLocalizedAt p` of $\mathbb{Q}$), and (iii) unramifiedness at every prime $q \notin S$. `TangentFinite` asserts the finiteness of the set of strict-equivalence classes (for the equivalence relation generated by [`GaloisRepAdic.IsEquiv`](def/GaloisRep_Adic.html#L125)) of those representations $\rho$ over the dual numbers $k[\varepsilon]$, viewed as an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra through $\mathcal{O} \to k \to k[\varepsilon]$, that satisfy `flatCondition 𝒪 p S` and whose residual representation is equivalent to the base change of $\bar\rho$ to the residue field of $k[\varepsilon]$. So: the flat tangent space of $\bar\rho$, in this quotient-set form, is finite.
--
--   Classically this is the statement that the tangent space of a deformation functor, i.e. its value on the dual numbers (Mazur), is finite-dimensional for the flat deformation problem of Wiles's Chapter 1; here the finiteness is asserted only as finiteness of a set of equivalence classes, with no linear structure and no bound, and nothing is claimed about existence of flat lifts of any given $\bar\rho$. It is one of the hypotheses of the project's representability theorem, and is used in that form in [`GaloisRep.nonempty_deformationRingData_flatCondition_and_isUnipotentOnInertiaAt`](thm.html#GaloisRep.nonempty_deformationRingData_flatCondition_and_isUnipotentOnInertiaAt) and, through it, in the construction of flat deformation data for semistable Weierstrass models.
